# File headers and JSDoc

New or substantially edited modules get a header. JSDoc every exported function.

```ts
/**
 * @file features/evm/lib/metrics.ts
 * @purpose Earned-value formulas (CPI, SPI, EAC)
 * @safe-to-edit CAREFUL
 * @affects manager dashboard, reports, S-curve
 * @depends-on features/evm/lib/rag-status.ts
 * @test-after-change npm run test:schedule
 */

/**
 * CPI = EV ÷ AC. Above 1 is favorable. Null when AC is not recorded.
 */
export function calculateCpi(ev: number, ac: number): number | null {
  if (!(ac > 0)) return null
  return ev / ac
}
```

`@safe-to-edit YES` only when changing the file cannot break others (pure config/labels).

Types for public data (no `any` on domain objects):

```ts
export interface EvmMetrics {
  bac: number
  pv: number
  ev: number
  ac: number
  cpi: number | null
  spi: number | null
}
```
